+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+The booking desk has no way to rent out boards and sails. The school needs a rental module, starting with the basics: register equipment, quote a rental, and book it without double-booking.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add an in-memory rental service, created with `createRentalService()` and exported from `src/index.ts`.
+- `addEquipment({ id, kind, dailyPrice })` registers a board or sail with a daily price in euro cents.
+- `quote({ itemId, start, end })` returns `{ itemId, start, end, total }`.
+- `book({ itemId, start, end })` books the item and returns `{ id, itemId, start, end, total }`.
+- Both `quote` and `book` throw for an unknown item or a disallowed period; `book` also throws when the item is not free for the whole period.
+- Record the cancellation policy as a requirement. Cancellation itself is **not** implemented in this change.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `rental-booking`: equipment registration, quoting and booking of whole-day rental periods, with money in integer euro cents, UTC times and no overlapping bookings of one item.
+- `rental-cancellation-policy`: the refund rule for cancelled bookings (no refund under 24 hours before start, otherwise full refund), recorded for later use.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+- New code under `src/` (none exists yet); `src/index.ts` becomes the package entry point.
+- No new runtime dependencies. No persistence: state is lost when the service is discarded.
